==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[Kory]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6~30 seconds<sup>180f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be easily [[Cheese]]d on all difficulties by simply spamming [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Wall/Eraser Cats]] for the entire level. If Li'l Wall is not in your possesion however, you can instead use his [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Normal counterpart]] to stall the starting peons and max out your wallet before starting the main show.

Tanky units like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] work well here. [[:Category:Midranger-class Cats|Midrange]]/[[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|Backline]] DPS units such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] are also helpful, though you'll need to be careful about using anything with lower range than them, since those units could act as stepping stones for Kory to fire off some Waves into them. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] can be used as a last resort by saving him until Kory nears the [[Cat Base]], then sending him out to land a quick knockback.

